    "description": "Vineyard Northeast is Vineyard Offshore's offshore wind development project for the New England market. The project is intended to serve utility-scale power demand in the region through future offshore wind procurement programs. The model is asset-heavy because it relies on federal lease rights, marine construction, transmission development, and large-scale project finance. Vineyard Offshore announced Vineyard Northeast in 2024 and associated the project with lease area OCS-A 0522. BOEM states that the OCS-A 0522 lease package went into effect on April 1, 2019, after Vineyard Wind, then a 50/50 Avangrid and Copenhagen Infrastructure Partners joint venture, won the 2018 auction. Public materials identify Vineyard Offshore as a CIP-supported platform, while the project-specific ownership percentage is not publicly disclosed.",
